  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Light rain showers and isolated dry thunderstorms\nare forecast today for the northeast portion of Elko County. No\nsignificant accumulation is expected under any such activity and\nrainfall totals will be around 0.10 inches or less. Otherwise, generally\nspeaking, weather will be fair thru the weekend. Daytime high temperatures\nwill also warm each day into Monday, returning to the upper 70s \nto mid 80s. \n\nA modest Pacific low is still on track to move thru southern \nNevada early next week. There is growing confidence in the\nprospect of rain showers and thunderstorms across central Nevada\nMonday and Tuesday. Rainfall accumulations look to be around 0.10\ninches but will almost certainly be variable across the region. Showers\nand thunderstorms likely spread north into Elko County by \nTuesday, though exactly how far north has yet to be determined. \n\nWeather will again become fair mid week under weak southwesterly\nflow. Latest numerical model solutions depict a deep Pacific trof\nmoving into the western U.S. in the Friday timeframe. An increase\nin south-southwesterly winds can be expected Friday and Saturday\nin response to the encroaching trof. Increasing probability of \nprecipitation is also expected late in the week under the \ninfluence of the trof. This is also in agreement with latest \nnumerical model solutions. Though will maintain a dry forecast at\nthis time until confidence in the prospect of rainfall becomes \nhigher.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: There is high confidence for showers\nand isolated thunderstorms today in northeast Elko County. Moderate\nconfidence for showers and thunderstorms in central Nevada Monday\nand Tuesday. Low confidence for the long range forecast as\nnumerical model solutions show a high degree of divergence for \nthe upper pattern late next week. Opted for a blend of various model\nguidance and NBM to produce a more realistic PoP and weather\nforecast thru the period. Adjusted overnight low temperatures a \nfew degrees colder in the typical colder valleys thru the weekend \ngiven mostly clear skies and enhanced radiative cooling.",
